# versions.env — the pinned versions for the spark-rocky build.
# Bump here to stay current, then rebuild 01->04 and re-verify (see docs/build/build.md).

# Kernel SOURCE selector -- the which-kernel knob. THE DEFAULT IS clk (Max, 2026-07-17): the shipped
# kernel is the CIQ Linux Kernel, GB10-validated end-to-end 2026-07-17 (boot, open driver, CUDA,
# 8 GiB managed memory). uname -r carries the lineage (e.g. 6.18.39-clk). kernelorg remains the A/B knob
# (stock kernel.org tarball, plain uname) -- one pin-flip away, parity receipts were recorded on it.
#   clk       = CIQ Linux Kernel from GitHub (CLK tree's own aarch64 config; release derived by make kernelrelease).
#   kernelorg = stock kernel.org tarball (the v-major path 6.x / 7.x is derived from KVER).
KERNEL_SOURCE=clk
KCONFIG=config/rocky-6.18.34-gb10.config   # kernelorg-path base .config (repo-relative; clk uses the CLK tree's own config). A/B knob.
# CLK commit to build from — THE SHIPPING PIN (KERNEL_SOURCE=clk is the default). This is the drift
# sensor's trigger row: refresh when ciq-6.18.y moves, not when kernel.org does. The commit SHA is the
# content anchor — git object addressing; the tarball URL is commit-addressed — which is a WEAKER model
# than kernelorg's GPG-signed sha256sums: GitHub archive bytes are not byte-stable, so no tarball hash
# can be pinned. The kernel release is derived by make kernelrelease (EXTRAVERSION empty on CLK stable
# branches; LOCALVERSION="-clk" is set by 01 for lineage).
# Branch: ciq-6.18.y  (the -dgx-spark-config-tweaks branch is RETIRED — DEVICE_PRIVATE proven not
# load-bearing on the coherent GB10, 2026-07-17; see #52.)
CLK_COMMIT=ceb41d6ec9bb0c8e28fdaf89fb5cec67790a5ee1   # 6.18.39 ("[CIQ] v6.18.39 - updated spec", 2026-07-20; #69)
KVER=6.18.38   # kernelorg A/B pin (NOT the shipping kernel since the clk default; sensor reports it as INFO)
DRIVER_VER=610.43.03
# SHA256 of NVIDIA-Linux-aarch64-$DRIVER_VER.run. NVIDIA publishes no signed checksums for the .run, so
# this pin is trust-on-first-download (TLS to us.download.nvidia.com + the .run's embedded `--check`
# self-test, both verified at bump time). What the pin buys: every rebuild consumes byte-identical driver
# input — a silent upstream re-roll or CDN tamper fails closed instead of silently changing the build.
# 02b verifies before extracting; 02c verifies before installing. Update when bumping DRIVER_VER.
DRIVER_SHA256=8d27655e8eb48a55cb2962af65f81b06756a558bb0eb38671ae883830c58cfde
ROCKY_RELEASEVER=10
# CUDA toolkit version for the IMAGE proof-of-life compiler (nvcc + cudart that validate.sh's vectorAdd uses).
# PINNED, not floating: held identical to the serving-container CUDA (13.0, #28) so the parity narrative in
# proof.md / software-stack.md stays true with zero edits, and a bump is a reviewable #26 diff -- never the
# silent package-name rot that 13-0 hardcoded in 02 used to be. This is NOT the parity CUDA; that lives in
# the digest-pinned serving containers and is out of scope for a live-USB release.
CUDA_VER=13-0
# Page size: PINNED. **4k as of 2026-07-17 — 64k REVERTED (#65/#66).** 64k was the opinionated default for
# the GB10 concurrent-serving workload (a measured win on 6.18.35), BUT a kernel regression from 6.18.37 on
# makes 64k FAULT the vLLM serve — a GPU Xid 31 MMU fault in the ~90 GB KV-cache allocation (#65). 4k is
# unaffected and serves clean on 6.18.38. Restore 64k once the upstream regression is bisected + fixed (#68).
# The page size is a kernel CONFIG choice (CONFIG_ARM64_4K_PAGES / _64K_PAGES), NOT a uname decoration: the
# kernel release stays plain $KVER either way, proven by the config symbol + getconf PAGESIZE + the
# provenance stamp, gated fail-closed in 05. Flip to 64k here (only) once #68 clears it.
PAGE_SIZE=4k
# SHA256 of linux-$KVER.tar.xz from kernel.org's signed sha256sums.asc (GPG-verified against the
# kernel.org autosigner key B886 8C80 BA62 A1FF FAF5 FDA9 632D 3A06 589D A6B1). 01-build-kernel.sh
# verifies the downloaded tarball against this before building (kernelorg only). Update when bumping KVER.
KERNEL_SHA256=ac26e508abd56e9f8b89872b6e10c49fc823bcc70d8068a5d8504c1a7c4ff045
